SMALLEST EXACT SHALLOW PROOF OBLIGATION
PEHD13: accepted + primitive + full residues + max(h)>=13 => a coordinate r with h_r>=13 and E_r subset D_(w_r-13).
iteration: PEHD13 -> height<=12 -> THM-770 dilation; THM-795 forbids a nonempty reverse lift chain.
equivalent regeneration target: an accepted primitive mechanical geodesic has only the single 46-chamber Farey-12 comb.
negative=first-tear time and THM-1010 max-speed descent are not valid potentials; containment must retain the whole essential stalk.

BRIDGE TO UNIFORM n=12 / COMPACT LRC14
positive=PEHD13 would close arbitrary winding in THM-769's shallow full-residue branch.
missing_after_PEHD13=THM-769 deep binding scales s>=2 (at least two off-sheet runners) remain separate.
compact=rho<13 plus the auxiliary 1/13 cover is a stronger sufficient compact target, not the full sharp LRC14 residual; PEHD13 feeds it only when a shallow 12-core is first forced.
therefore=no valid direct inference from the h<=3 certificate to sporadic emptiness or INVcov.

